Q {"id": "Q12", "question": "What are the rewards and reversibility at 2 and 4 Faction Influence, and does tying the Alliance holder at 4 steal the Alliance?"}
KEY {"id": "Q12", "expected_answer": "Reach 2 gets 1 VP lost below 2. Reach 4 gets track bonus retained if falling below, can earn again on re-reaching. First to 4 gets Alliance and its VP; tie does not steal, opponent must rise higher. Transfer loses old holder VP and gives new holder VP.", "source_references": "Main p7 / extraction 333–344", "novelty": "Influence thresholds and Alliance"}
A {"id": "Q12", "answer": "At 2 Influence, gain 1 VP; falling below 2 loses it, and reaching 2 again regains it. At 4, gain the printed track bonus, which is retained after falling below 4 and earned again on returning to 4; the first player to 4 also gets the Alliance token and its 1 VP, which remains only while holding the token. Tying the holder at 4 does not transfer it: a challenger must rise above the holder. The FAQ also says if the holder loses Influence after having been tied, the formerly tied opponent takes it (or, if several were tied, the former holder chooses); if nobody has 4+ when holder falls to 3 or less, return the token to the board.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Faction Influence: separate reversal rules for track bonus and Alliance VP; tying does not steal; FAQ transfer triggers described."}
B {"id": "Q12", "answer": "At 2 Influence, gain 1 VP; lose that VP below 2 and regain it upon reaching 2 again. At 4, gain the printed track bonus, which is retained if Influence falls below 4 and earned again on returning to 4. The first to 4 also gets the Alliance token and its 1 VP, which stays only while holding the token. Tying the holder does not steal it: a challenger must rise above them (or the separate FAQ holder-loss trigger can transfer it).", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Faction Influence scoring: 2 VP reverses below 2; 4 track bonus retained; Alliance tied to holder, ties don't steal; rising above transfers."}
