A {"id": "Q14", "answer": "At the Makers phase, add 1 spice to each unoccupied Maker space’s bonus spot; accumulated bonus spice remains until an Agent visits, and the visitor gains all of it, including when choosing worms. Deep Desert costs 3 water and offers 4 base spice or, with Maker Hooks, two worms; Hagga Basin costs 1 water and offers 2 base spice or, with Hooks, one worm. Hooks are required only when the summoning effect specifies them and are retained, not spent. While the Shield Wall remains, worms cannot be summoned to Arrakeen, Spice Refinery or Imperial Basin; removing the Wall allows summoning to any Conflict. A sandworm is placed directly in your Conflict quadrant and never in a garrison.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Makers; Sandworms; Maker Reward Doubling sections; Deep Desert/Hagga table: bonus spice gained on visit; Wall protects three locations; worms never in garrison."}
